{"title":"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Complementary_Counting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One fair die has faces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3edba73de83c04ddb17557dbf5235fa6fafbf8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" /> and another has faces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/5471e1cff7938524f987c64bffc8e405303939da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 4, 5, 5, 6, 6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" /> The dice are rolled and the numbers on the top faces are added. What is the probability that the sum will be odd?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd7028b71e1a7f1a73afa1d30750d7d9ff2e1041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{4}{9} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{5}{9} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"375\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to obtain an odd sum, exactly one out of the two dice must have an odd number. We can easily find the total probability using casework.\n</p><p><b>Case 1</b>: The first die is odd and the second die is even.\n</p><p>The probability of this happening is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/708fe26ecce68bf2ea450750d9c01c31a79274a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{4}{6}\\times\\dfrac{4}{6}=\\dfrac{16}{36}=\\dfrac{4}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"130\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><b>Case 2</b>: The first die is even and the second die is odd.\n</p><p>The probability of this happening is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/42668f582f25cdc202d85af2631cf08c0bda07b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2}{6}\\times\\dfrac{2}{6}=\\dfrac{4}{36}=\\dfrac{1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"130\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Adding these two probabilities will give us our final answer. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d6ca94aedcd33edc5c7f409b228870fb0965e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{4}{9}+\\dfrac{1}{9}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\dfrac{5}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"135\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>If you run out of time, you can see it is obviously greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> so it narrows guesses.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Complementary_Counting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Complementary_Counting)\">Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see can see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to get an even number, and other ways get us an odd. Therefore, if we subtract the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/9/7195ac82ad7635889e2c7c07f93a8a383d88423f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\text{even})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />, we will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f309bddf66e7cc67597fe9a44f7f4f60c23bae75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\text{odd})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />. We can get an even either by getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> evens or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> odds. Both cases give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041a0b37ca609642fb34c7c855b9d67ed498a560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f309bddf66e7cc67597fe9a44f7f4f60c23bae75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\text{odd})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0fe1e65a30f9ca06db19560db6eb8b1f6ff1f10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2 \\cdot \\frac{2}{9}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{5}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"153\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B\">2005 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n<